<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39562" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικάμπ-τω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bend into an angle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δάκτυλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					556b17
				</span></i>
			; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλάδους] χερσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					21.249a
				</span></i>
			; Archit., <i>make an</i>
			<i>angle</i> or <i>return,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				22.1668.75
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>bend</i> or <i>turn</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὰ ἀριστερά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Oss.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			; <i>arch</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρὺς ἐπικεκαμμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>PA</u>
					671b33
				</span></i>
			; of troops, <i>advance the wings, so as to form angles</i>
			with the centre and take the enemy in flank, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.1.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HG</u>
				4.2.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.</u>
				1.8.23
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ στόμα ἐπικεκαμμένον</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχουσα [φάλαγξ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				11.1
			</span></i>; also of a fleet, <i>form</i>
			<i>a curved line</i> so as to envelop the enemy, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				50.31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. 
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ</span>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἔλεόν τινας</span>
			<i>move</i> to pity, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				46.13
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, abs., <i><span class="en">
				Ctes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				29.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				6.38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὸν ὀδυρμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Loc.</u>
					1.31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. intr.,
				<i>to be bent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				529a12
			</span></i>.</div>
